{"version":"1","id":"bootstrap","handle":"bootstrap","name":"Bootstrap","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/ea4f1ba8a2d6493e853e77a6002c9c00","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-8.7815,"y":2.8992,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":47,"newest_post_at":"2025-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-12-07T11:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":2.5625,"summary_length_avg":285.288889,"title_length_avg":19.085106,"title_length_var":20.801268,"tag_entropy":2.315965,"tag_diversity":0.404255,"top_tag_share":0.212766,"avg_upvotes":13.468085,"median_upvotes":8.0,"avg_comments":0.702128,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.053628,"zero_engagement_share":0.085106,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.191006,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.068182},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.8676,4.7059],"cadence_depth":[-4.7059,-7.0],"hype_variety":[-9.1176,-7.7206],"title_style":[-9.1176,-8.6029]},"top_tags":[["bootstrap-css",28],["css",20],["bootstrap",18],["github",9],["web-design",7],["webdev",6],["javascript",4],["figma",3]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Bootstrap 5.3.6","Bootstrap 5.3.4","Bootstrap 5.3.7"],"outlier":["Using CSS variables in Bootstrap"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"oMQ3pEZnC","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.8","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/08/25/bootstrap-5-3-8/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-8-omq3peznc","summary":"Bootstrap 5.3.8 has been released as the final patch before version 5.4.0. This update reverts a dropdown focus bug, includes CSS improvements for WCAG 2.1 compliance and spinner distortion fixes, and removes references to the discontinued Bootstrap Themes site. The release focuses primarily on bug fixes and documentation updates rather than new features.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":36,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"KRYowDmnb","title":"GitHub Secure Open Source Fund","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/08/10/github-secure-open-source-fund/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/github-secure-open-source-fund-kryowdmnb","summary":"Bootstrap maintainers participated in GitHub's Secure Open Source Fund program, a three-week intensive training focused on improving security and sustainability of open source projects. The program covered threat modeling, secure GitHub Actions, incident response planning, and vulnerability management through expert-led sessions and workshops. As a result, Bootstrap implemented immediate security improvements including SBOM analysis, private vulnerability reporting, and fuzzing experiments, while planning longer-term initiatives like incident response plans and threat modeling.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"bCrqynQzP","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.7","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/06/17/bootstrap-5-3-7/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-7-bcrqynqzp","summary":"Bootstrap 5.3.7 has been released with follow-up fixes from the Astro migration and various small improvements. Key updates include documentation fixes for broken GitHub URLs and HTML head content, improved accessibility features, refined sanitizer documentation, and better floating labels usage. The release also consolidates Sass box-shadow mixin values, fixes popover and tooltip behavior issues, and adds recommended VSCode extensions configuration to the repository.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":47,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2025-06-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"CHCQQY5Th","title":"Bootstrap Icons v1.12 and v1.13","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/05/09/bootstrap-icons-1-12-1-13/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-icons-v1-12-and-v1-13-chcqqy5th","summary":"Recent Bootstrap Icons updates include v1.12, featuring a single new icon, and v1.13, introducing several more icons, Sass file guidance with Vite, and bug fixes. Additionally, a hotfix for the documentation search issue was addressed in v1.13.1. The Figma file has been made more accessible through the Figma Community.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"qyniBPxB7","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.6","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/05/05/bootstrap-5-3-6/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-6-qynibpxb7","summary":"Bootstrap 5.3.6 has been released with significant updates, including migrating documentation from Hugo to Astro, improved usage docs for Accordion JavaScript, and fixes for .visually-hidden and .card-group elements. Acknowledgments are given to maintainer Julien for efforts on the Astro migration.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":73,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2025-05-05T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"inJLdFFk2","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.5","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/04/04/bootstrap-5-3-5/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-5-injldffk2","summary":"Bootstrap version 5.3.5 has been released to address a regression issue from Autoprefixer that caused floating form labels to always be 'floated' in Firefox. This release includes several documentation and dependency updates. The update is available on the Bootstrap website and on npm.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":37,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-04T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"VFwc6PgA0","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.4","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2025/04/03/bootstrap-5-3-4/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-4-vfwc6pga0","summary":"Bootstrap v5.3.4 includes several bug fixes and documentation updates. Notable changes involve fixes for modal and offcanvas headers, close button display issues in color modes, light mode carousel, floating label alignment for select elements, Sass 1.77.7 deprecation, and popover toggling. Visit the GitHub changelog for a detailed list of changes and head to the official site for the latest version.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":64,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2025-04-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"1hWHk5FHW","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.3","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2024/02/20/bootstrap-5-3-3/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-3-1hwhk5fhw","summary":"Bootstrap 5.3.3 has been released with bug fixes, documentation improvements, and enhancements for color modes. The release fixes a breaking change with color modes and a regression in the selector engine. Additionally, it introduces improvements to the color modes and miscellaneous fixes and enhancements.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":24,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2024-02-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"hGXoCjdIz","title":"Bootstrap 5.3.2","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2023/09/14/bootstrap-5-3-2/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-5-3-2-hgxocjdiz","summary":"Bootstrap 5.3.2 is here with bug fixes, documentation improvements, and more follow-up enhancements for color modes. Highlights: Passing a percentage unit to the global is deprecated since Dart Sass v1.65.0.0. It resulted in a deprecation warning when compiling Bootstrap with Dart Sass.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":17,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-09-14T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"JoYoBOlW3","title":"Bootstrap Icons v1.11.0","url":"https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2023/09/12/bootstrap-icons-1-11-0/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bootstrap-icons-v1-11-0-joyobolw3","summary":"Bootstrap Icons v1.11.0 has arrived with 100 new icons. New floppy disk icons, additional brand icons, new person icons and new emojis have been added. We\u2019re now at over 2,000 icons! Here's a quick look at all the new icons.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36bacccb6f9846dad141a3901cf287ac?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-12T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["weeklyvuenews","asayer","zaidesanton","csstip","bram"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_"],"similar":[{"id":"weeklyvuenews","handle":"weeklyvuenews","name":"Weekly Vue News","is_squad":false,"x":-8.6986,"y":2.9665,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":149,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/fb57a3aa473141c6bc2c120fd4785a99","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.939579,"median_upvotes":10.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.003356,"avg_read_time":1.120805,"tag_diversity":0.281879},"top_tags_preview":[["vuejs",141],["webdev",80],["nuxt",78]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.4853,-4.7059],"cadence_depth":[1.6176,-9.0441],"hype_variety":[-2.3824,-7.25],"title_style":[-4.0441,-0.5147]}},{"id":"asayer","handle":"asayer","name":"asayer","is_squad":false,"x":-8.7837,"y":2.6491,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":589,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/be8d9d38650943c8a1718ba79f23e9ac","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":3.514097,"median_upvotes":14.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.011036,"avg_read_